---@return any
function mods.call(mod, name, ...) end

--- Raises an event in every other mod: their events.on handlers get the values after the running handler (in this frame or the next). Prefix the name with your mod's id.
---@param event string 
---@param ... any plain data
function mods.emit(event, ...) end

--- Shift-JIS bytes (packets, game files) as text.
---@param bytes string 
---@return string
function text.from_shift_jis(bytes) end

--- Text as Shift-JIS bytes.
---@param text string 
---@return string
function text.to_shift_jis(text) end

--- An auto-translate phrase as a line holds it (group, id from res.autotranslate); put it in chat text.
---@param group integer 
---@param id integer 
---@return string
function text.phrase(group, id) end

--- The phrase whose text is exactly `text` (ignoring case and spaces at the ends; a group title matches too), as a line holds it; nil when the dictionary has none.
---@param text string 
---@return string?
function text.autotranslate(text) end

--- A line without its in-line codes (colours, indents): the words alone.
---@param text string 
---@return string
function text.strip(text) end

--- `text` in the log's in-line colour code `code` (as the game colours names: 7 ours, 6 party, 3 alliance, 8 a monster we claimed, 5 another's), then back to the line's own colour; 0 leaves it.
---@param text string 
---@param code integer 
---@return string
function text.colour(text, code) end

--- A line with its auto-translate phrases as plain words.
---@param text string 
---@return string
function text.plain(text) end

--- Puts text on the clipboard.
---@param text string 
function client.copy(text) end

--- Reads the clipboard's text after this frame and hands it to the handler. Needs clipboard.
---@param handler fun(text: string) 
function client.paste(handler) end

--- The HID devices: {path, vendor, product, name, interface (the USB interface, when known), descriptor (the report descriptor's bytes, Linux)}. On Linux the hidraw nodes (opening one needs read and write access to it); on Windows the HID interfaces (the system holds keyboards and mice itself). Needs devices.
---@return table[]
function devices.list() end

--- Opens a device by its path; handlers {open(id), data(id, report), close(id, error?)} run in later mod phases, one data call a report (the report id first where the device numbers them). Returns its id. Needs devices.
---@param path string 
---@param handlers table 
---@return integer
function devices.open(path, handlers) end

--- Sends an output report (its report id first, 0 when the device has none; on Windows exactly the report's length). Needs devices.
---@param id integer 
---@param report string 
function devices.write(id, report) end

--- Closes a device.
---@param id integer 
function devices.close(id) end

--- Records the game window as drawn to an H.264 video (ffmpeg must be installed) under the client's ffxiuser/videos folder, as `name`.mp4 (the date and time when none; -2, -3... when that file exists): options {fps (30)}. It ends with stop_recording, a new recording by this mod, a new window size, or the mod unloading; no sound. Another mod's recording running is an error; a start that fails puts the reason in the chat log. Returns the file's path. Needs exec.
---@param name? string 
---@param options? {fps: integer?} 
---@return string
function client.record(name, options) end

--- Ends this mod's recording (ffmpeg finishes the file).
function client.stop_recording() end

--- The file being recorded, or nil (as of the last frame).
---@return string?
function client.recording() end

--- The client's process: pid, cores (the computer's, whatever the affinity), affinity (the cores it may run on, from 0; empty where unknown) and priority (idle, low, below_normal, normal, above_normal, high).
---@return {pid: integer, cores: integer, affinity: integer[], priority: string}
function client.process() end

--- Runs every thread of the client on these cores (from 0). Needs process. Returns true, or false and why.
---@param cores integer[] 
---@return boolean, string?
function client.set_affinity(cores) end

--- The client's scheduling priority: idle, low, below_normal, normal, above_normal or high (above normal usually needs privileges on Linux). Needs process. Returns true, or false and why.
---@param level string 
---@return boolean, string?
function client.set_priority(level) end

--- A behaviour switch's value (see set_option); a value set shows from the next frame.
---@param name string 
---@return boolean|number|table
function client.option(name) end

--- Sets a behaviour switch while the mod is loaded (the game's usual behaviour back when it unloads): macro_palette_delay (false: the Ctrl / Alt palette opens at once, not at the next whole second), ah_result_delay (false: a bid's result prints at once), equipset_delay (false: no 0.9 s wait between equip sets), log_slide (false: new log lines show at once), cutscene_speed (1..4: events play that much faster), animation_rate (0.25..4: the actors' animation speed), clear_colour and ambient ({r, g, b} 0..255 in place of the zone's background colour and ambient light; false gives the zone's back), minimap_span (the minimap's zoom, map pixels across, 48..512; kept as the minimap's own wheel keeps it); rules: move_lock (false: our abilities' and the weapon draw's move lock is lifted), all_maps (true: every map without its key item), dead_commands (true: text commands while K.O.), compass_monsters (true: monster dots on the compass for every job), player_collision (false: moving players never hold a step), occlusion (false: characters behind scenery still draw and target), menu_reach (false: the auction house and the nomad moogle menu stay open as we move away); send_interval (ms between the datagrams we send, 50..1000; the game's is 400); wireframe (true: the scenery drawn as lines, where the GPU draws them); ttf_text (true: the game font's text in the UI's TrueType face in the classic UI too: the log, the windows' text; sprite numbers and captions stay as the game draws them); stamp_all_lines (true: the game's chat timestamps on every log line, not only chat; with them off, hours, minutes and seconds); synth_amount (true: after Synthesize the synthesis window asks how many, 1 to the sets held, and gives the count to the mods' synth_amount event). A value of the wrong type is an error.
---@param name string 
---@param value boolean|number|table 
function client.set_option(name, value) end

--- The game window: {x, y (its place on the desktop, when the system tells it), w, h (pixels), focused}.
---@return {x: integer?, y: integer?, w: integer, h: integer, focused: boolean}
function client.window() end

--- Changes the game window: moves ({x, y}), sizes ({w, h}), top (always on top), minimised, fullscreen (borderless, on its monitor), border (the system frame), capture = false (kept out of screen captures where the system allows it). Only the fields given change. Needs multibox.
---@param window {x: integer?, y: integer?, w: integer?, h: integer?, top: boolean?, minimised: boolean?, fullscreen: boolean?, border: boolean?, capture: boolean?} 
function client.set_window(window) end

--- Asks for the keyboard focus for this game window (switching between clients). Needs multibox.
function client.focus() end

--- Saves a screenshot of the next frame as drawn, under the game's screenshots folder (subfolders allowed; .png added); returns the name used.
---@param name? string 
---@return string
function client.screenshot(name) end

--- Starts a program with its arguments (no shell). With a handler, it gets {status (the exit code; minus the signal's number for a program a signal ended), body (stdout), headers = {stderr}} when the program ends, or {error}. Returns the process id. Needs exec.
---@param program string 
---@param args? string[] 
---@param handler? fun(result: table) 
---@return integer
function client.run(program, args, handler) end

--- Writes storage.account and storage.character now (they are also written at logout and unload).
function storage.save() end

--- Seals text (a password) with this machine's key, for storage: only this mod on this machine can open it.
---@param text string 
---@return string
function storage.seal(text) end

--- Opens text storage.seal made; nil when it does not open (another machine or mod, or damaged).
---@param sealed string 
---@return string?
function storage.unseal(sealed) end

--- The lobby before login (a mod with `lobby = true` in mod.toml runs there): screen (login, title, select, create, delete, config, connecting, world), server, account, playonline, busy (a fade, a reply awaited or an error up: actions wait), error, selected (a slot) and characters {slot, name, world, race, job, level, sub_job, zone, available}.
---@return table
function lobby.state() end

--- Signs in from the login screen as its Log in button does: {account, password, otp?, server?}, and for a PlayOnline server pol_id and pol_password. Needs automation.
---@param login table 
function lobby.sign_in(login) end

--- Logs in with a character from any character screen (title, select...) while the lobby is not busy, as the select screen's Play does: its name or its slot. Needs automation.
---@param character string|integer 
function lobby.play(character) end

--- A setting declared in mod.toml: the user's value, else its default.
---@param key string 
---@return any
function settings.get(key) end

-- Events (events.on):
--   load(): The mod's entry file has run.
--   unload(): The mod is about to be unloaded (logout, /lua unload or reload; a lobby mod as the client closes).
--   login(name: string): The character is in the world, once per session.
--   lobby_screen(screen: string, previous: string?): The lobby's screen changed (see lobby.state; world once in the world). Lobby mods get it from the start.
--   logout(): The character is leaving the world.
--   zone_change(zone: integer, previous: integer?): A new zone has loaded.
--   settings_changed(key: string, value: any): The user changed one of the mod's settings (its Extras page, or /lua set).
--   focus_change(focused: boolean): The game window gained or lost the keyboard focus.
--   emote(actor: integer, target: integer, emote: integer, mode: integer): Someone used an emote (s2c 0x05A): who, at whom (0 none), the emote id, its mode (motion only, text only...).
--   party_invite(from: string, kind: 'party'|'alliance'): We were invited to a party or an alliance (s2c 0x0DC).
--   examined(id: integer, name: string): Someone examined us (/check; message 89).
--   frame(dt: number): Every frame (prefer timers and events: this one costs time every frame).
--   hp_change(hp: integer, previous: integer): Our HP changed.
--   mp_change(mp: integer, previous: integer): Our MP changed.
--   tp_change(tp: integer, previous: integer): Our TP changed.
--   hpp_change(hpp: integer, previous: integer): Our HP percent changed.
--   mpp_change(mpp: integer, previous: integer): Our MP percent changed.
--   status_change(status: integer, previous: integer): Our status changed (0 idle, 1 engaged, 2 / 3 dead, 33 resting...).
--   job_change(main: integer, main_level: integer, sub: integer, sub_level: integer): Our main or sub job changed.
--   level_up(level: integer): Our main job's level went up.
--   level_down(level: integer): Our main job's level went down.
--   buff_gain(id: integer): We gained a status effect.
--   buff_lose(id: integer): We lost a status effect.
--   target_change(id: integer?, previous: integer?): Our target changed (nil: none).
--   time_change(minute: integer, previous: integer): A Vana'diel minute passed (minutes since midnight).
--   day_change(weekday: integer, previous: integer): A new Vana'diel day (0 Firesday).
--   moon_change(phase: integer, previous: integer): The moon's phase changed.
--   weather_change(weather: integer, previous: integer): The weather changed.
--   party_change(): The party or alliance changed (members joined, left or moved).
--   item_add(bag: integer, slot: integer, id: integer, count: integer): An item appeared in a bag slot.
--   item_remove(bag: integer, slot: integer, id: integer, count: integer): An item left a bag slot.
--   chat_message(text: string, sender: string, kind: integer, gm: boolean): A chat line from a player (or a GM): its text, sender, kind (0 say, 1 shout, 3 tell, 4 party, 5 linkshell, 0x1a yell, 0x1b linkshell 2, 0x21 unity) and whether a GM sent it.
--   action(action: vana.Action): A decoded action packet (s2c 0x028): actor, category, param, info and targets with their results.
--   battle_message(actor: integer, target: integer, message: integer, param1: integer, param2: integer): A battle message (s2c 0x029 / 0x02D): actor, target, message id and its two parameters.
--   suggestions(rows: table[]): The client's suggestion rules picked new rows for the modern battle menu (while it is open and a mod listens; none when it closes): a list of battle_rows rows ({kind, id, target, reason, label, group}); held still while the cursor is on one of them, only its submenu's spells retaken.
--   synth_amount(count: integer, recipe: table): The synthesis window's count step (client option synth_amount) was answered: the first synthesis has gone out; recipe = {crystal, items (one material id per unit)} for actions.synth.
--   synth_result(result: integer, item: integer, count: integer, grade: integer): Our synthesis was answered (s2c 0x06F): result 0 and 12 made, 1 failed (materials lost); others refused or cut short (the reason's line printed); item, count, grade (0 normal, 1..3 high quality) of what was made.
--   zone_text(id: integer, actor: integer, plain: boolean, packet: integer): A zone dialogue line came (s2c 0x036 / 0x02A / 0x027): its id in the install (res.zone_text), its actor, whether MesNum's bit 15 marks it plain, the packet.
--   damage(actor: integer, target: integer, value: integer, message: integer): A damage number: a battle message that puts one up (main and proc records), whatever the chat filters show.
--   ipc_message(text: string, from: string): Text the same mod sent from another game window on this machine (ipc.send; needs multibox).
--   item_change(bag: integer, slot: integer, id: integer, count: integer, previous: integer): A bag slot's count changed.
